1540: Its local rings are therefore torsion free
1541: over the one-dimensional parameter ring,
1542: which proves flatness over the \(v\)-disc.
1543: 
1544: ## 23. Remaining original-u cap-root endpoint dictionary
1545: 
1546: Sections 19--22 construct the literal marked \((v,T)\) family,
1547: with its cap root defined by \(z_{\rm new}^m=T^{-1}\).
1548: The comparison to a source loop in the original normalized
1549: \((u,t)\) presentation retains a further root arrow. The exact
1550: source map is
1551: \[
1552:  (X,Y,T,v)=(u^2x,u^3y,u^4t,u^3),\qquad
1553:                    z_{\rm old}^m=u^4z_{\rm new}^m.     \tag{SZ.52}
1554: \]
1555: Thus a full positive original \(u\)-loop covers three positive
1556: \(v\)-loops, and the continued root comparison has the
1557: additional rotation \(z_{\rm old}\mapsto\zeta_m^4z_{\rm old}\).
1558: This is an actual root-coordinate factor, rather than a bounded
1559: unit with a chosen logarithm on the full puncture.
1560: 
1561: The generic suspension square is already exact. Under the
1562: source and Cartier coordinate isomorphism \(I_u\),
1563: \[
1564:  I_u U_{a,\rm old}I_u^{-1}=u^{2a}U_{a,\rm new},\qquad
1565:  q_{\rm old}=u^{-4}q_{\rm new}.
1566: \]
1567: Since \(ab=2\), the factors cancel in
1568: \[
1569:  2(-1)^{b+1}\lambda q_{\rm old}U_{a,\rm old}^{\,b}.
1570: \]
1571: Consequently this ordinary comparison retains the same scalar
1572: \(\lambda\). The finite-cap character and its actual norm lift
1573: must still be carried through the root rotation in (SZ.52).
1574: No equality of their endpoint maps follows from the displayed
1575: ordinary cancellation alone.
1576: 
1577: The remaining typed square has the old cap on the root
1578: \(z_{\rm old}^m=t^{-1}\), the new cap on
1579: \(z_{\rm new}^m=T^{-1}\), and the source/Cartier map (SZ.52).
1580: It must intertwine the actual \(A_0\), its division-section
1581: branch, and its finite line character, including the
1582: \(\zeta_m^4\) endpoint. Until this square is written,
1583: the audited analytic quotient in Section 22 retains its
1584: specified \((v,T)\) marking. It assigns neither an original
1585: \(u\)-loop return nor a numerical \(v\)-loop return.
